# POINTS: a catalogued code closed over captures
# that are not the definitional ones. A closure is its code and
# its captures, and the same code over another capture is another
# function; a replacement keyed by the code's address must check every
# capture, or fall back when one is not the definitional one. Written as
# traps, points of the boolean format of
# contest_hidden_fourth.pl: the scored claim is the definitional
# boolean, the trap the one a replacement that ignores the captures
# answers, the proof the finite head class with the derivation at the
# fact.
#
# - hidden_capture_equal_self_K_N: natural_equal's generator (the
#   prelude's `fixpoint @ Generator`) closed over a bounded Self, S_K N N
#   with S_0 = \a. \b. false and S_K = Generator S_(K-1), N > K. Its
#   inner code is the catalogue's natural_equal inner code with another
#   Self. S_K N N unfolds K times to S_0 (N-K) (N-K) = false. A
#   replacement that reads real equality answers true.
# - hidden_capture_times_plus_A_B: the label-free times body closed over
#   a plus that answers zero for every pair, applied to A = 2^k and
#   B > 0, tested for zero. Its innermost code is the catalogue's
#   merge_binary_times address with another Plus. The definitional times
#   doubles k times and then answers the fake sum, zero, so the product
#   is zero and the test true. A replacement that reads real
#   multiplication answers 2^k B > 0, false.
#
# The sizes reach the native code (measured: at K >= 3 and
# A >= 64 the lazy JIT enters the code natively and a replacement is
# asked; below, none is).
#
# Readings at main 81bc1856c, 2026-09-28: under weak_head
# and tabling(weak_head) every scored claim is answered within 6 ms and
# every trap fails. Under native_replacements(native_solved(
# lazily_specialised([extent(8), key(shape), entry(native)], weak_head)))
# every trap succeeds (a false positive) and every scored claim fails;
# so does a setting that names the replacements, on the
# two natural_equal points.
#
# TARGET ALGORITHMS, the specific known algorithms the problem targets, each
# with its prior work:
# - recognising catalogued code by the content address of its normal form,
#   as hash-consing shares equal terms: J.-C. Filliâtre, S. Conchon,
#   Type-Safe Modular Hash-Consing, ML Workshop 2006,
#   doi:10.1145/1159876.1159880.
# - a closure is its code and its captures, the representation a replacement
#   must inspect before it trusts the code's address: J. C. Reynolds,
#   Definitional Interpreters for Higher-Order Programming Languages,
#   Higher-Order and Symbolic Computation 1998, doi:10.1023/A:1010027404223.
# - replacing recognised code by a native implementation is a rewrite by a
#   library law, applied only where its side condition (the domain check)
#   holds: R. Tate, M. Stepp, Z. Tatlock, S. Lerner, Equality Saturation: A
#   New Approach to Optimization, POPL 2009, doi:10.1145/1480881.1480915.

#
# The value is a constructor of schema/intended_value, here `boolean` of a
# Church Boolean of corpora/library/prelude/boolean. Each other text is
# from_cbor of a string literal, a Scott list of bytes, imported from
# corpora/library/text/cbor. FIXME: the imports project "corpora" https://github.com/Atry/private-overlay/issues/1923
# off the variable gezi, the name of the project root's own
# directory; it breaks if that directory is renamed.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "text") "cbor")
λ text_from_cbor _ _ _
. (λtuple. tuple λ. text_from_cbor λx. x)
λ text
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "schema") "intended_value")
λ boolean _ _ _
. export
λ
. cons
  ( λ _capture_trap
    . _capture_trap (text "hidden_capture_equal_self_three_five") (boolean false)
    λ
    . text "S_3 5 5 unfolds natural_equal's generator three times, each step taking both numerals to their predecessors, to S_0 2 2 = (\\a. \\b. false) 2 2 = false"
  )
λ
. cons
  ( λ _capture_trap
    . _capture_trap (text "hidden_capture_equal_self_ten_twelve") (boolean false)
    λ
    . text "S_10 12 12 unfolds natural_equal's generator ten times, each step taking both numerals to their predecessors, to S_0 2 2 = (\\a. \\b. false) 2 2 = false"
  )
λ
